# L §8.2 One read set (tally 2.1.7 R7, #146; the fix review's defect B, pick P45): "an entry is listed under a result
# exactly when a read in its set gives it", and each line of a fan-out is a result. In t5 and t1 the k1 line reads r[k1]
# under the ask's with pin, the k2 line under an inner as if alone: the pin is listed on the k1 line only. refcore after
# P41 kept one record of the pins reads took per ask, so the k2 line listed it too.
=== m.tally
model c7
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented"
index ks = [k1, k2]
input r[k in ks]: num
input seven: num
def one: num = r[k1] at reader

ask t5: (if k == k2 then (one as if {r[k1] = 3}) else one) for k in ks with r[k1] = 9 law 2026-06-30
ask t1: (if k == k2 then (one as if {r[k1] = seven}) else one) for k in ks with r[*] = 9 law 2026-06-30

version v
  cite card
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  r[*] = 1
  seven = 7
=== expect
t1 (k = k1): 9
  pinned: r[*] = 9
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
t1 (k = k2): 7
  pinned: r[k1] = 7
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
t5 (k = k1): 9
  pinned: r[k1] = 9
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
t5 (k = k2): 3
  pinned: r[k1] = 3
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
